    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="1167" n="1033" xml:id="pg1033"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Bulgaria)/6–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 693 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State ad interim
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d693-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-29T17:00:00+02:00">June 29, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2814. Gen Oxley head Brit delegation
                        ACC
                    Bulgaria … has just returned from tour
                    Sofia to Varna. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>
                    Oxley found that everyone he met spoke
                    freely of Russian aspirations in Dardanelles. As illustration of this widespread
                    opinion Oxley mentioned meeting drunken
                    Russian corporal who expressed greatest delight at meeting Brit party and said
                    he has just been told English had agreed to Russians having Dardanelles in
                    return for free hand in Austria. Bulgarian civilians cannot understand why
                    Bulgarian Army is not being demobilized; in fact officers cadre is being
                    increased.</p>
                <p>
                    Oxley’s summary impression was that
                    Russian forces are massing in depth north from Greek and Turk frontiers.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d693-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
